<h2>How to use this portal</h2>
<p>Every phase of a client project is documented as its own page in the sidebar. Each page follows the same shape: <strong>goal</strong>, <strong>trigger</strong>, <strong>who's involved</strong>, <strong>steps</strong>, <strong>templates</strong>, <strong>common issues</strong>, <strong>exit criteria</strong>. Use the prev/next pager at the bottom of each page to walk through a project end-to-end.</p>

<div class="sop-callout">
  <div>
    <strong>Confidentiality</strong>
    Every page in this portal carries <code>noindex</code> + is disallowed in <code>robots.txt</code>. Don't paste contents into Slack, public docs, or AI chat windows that train on inputs. Treat client examples as PII unless explicitly cleared.
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Project lifecycle at a glance</h2>
<p>A typical engagement runs about four to six weeks from first contact to launch, then continues indefinitely on the monthly plan. Phases overlap; this is a checklist, not a Gantt chart.</p>

<div class="sop-meta">
  <div><strong>Average time to launch</strong> 4-6 weeks from discovery call</div>
  <div><strong>Median revisions</strong> 2 design rounds, 1 build round</div>
  <div><strong>SLA, content updates</strong> same business day</div>
  <div><strong>SLA, emergencies</strong> &lt; 1 hour business hrs / &lt; 4 hrs after-hours</div>
</div>

<h2>The 12 phases</h2>
<ol style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.85rem;list-style:none;padding:0;max-width:none">
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/first-contact/">01 &middot; First contact</a>.</strong> Inbound lead handling: where they came from, qualifying triage, when to advance vs decline.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/discovery-call/">02 &middot; Discovery call</a>.</strong> 20-minute call. Script, qualification questions, fit assessment, what to send next.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/proposal-agreement/">03 &middot; Proposal &amp; agreement</a>.</strong> Quote, contract, deposit (if any), signed agreement returned, project repo created.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/onboarding/">04 &middot; Onboarding</a>.</strong> Kickoff email, asset collection (logo, photos, copy), expectations, project kickoff scheduled.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/design/">05 &middot; Design</a>.</strong> Wireframe to high-fidelity preview. Feedback loop. Sign-off before build starts.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/build/">06 &middot; Build</a>.</strong> Code the design. Performance + accessibility throughout. Internal QA between rounds.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/pre-launch-qa/">07 &middot; Pre-launch QA</a>.</strong> Full audit before go-live: links, Lighthouse, accessibility, content, schema, mobile.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/launch/">08 &middot; Launch</a>.</strong> DNS migration, Search Console submission, monitoring setup, post-launch checks.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/maintenance/">09 &middot; Maintenance</a>.</strong> Ongoing content updates, ticket triage, monthly check-ins.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/emergencies/">10 &middot; Emergencies</a>.</strong> What counts, response SLA, communication protocol, post-incident.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/billing/">11 &middot; Billing &amp; invoicing</a>.</strong> Monthly invoice cycle, late payments, plan changes, refunds, write-offs.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/offboarding/">12 &middot; Offboarding</a>.</strong> Clean-exit playbook when a client leaves: handoff bundle, internal cleanup, posture.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Marketing &amp; growth playbook</h2>
<p>The 12 lifecycle phases above process inbound work. The 11 marketing SOPs below generate it. Each one is a system that runs on a defined cadence, regardless of whether the pipeline currently feels full or empty.</p>
<ol style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.65rem;list-style:none;padding:0;max-width:none">
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/cold-outreach/">M1 &middot; Cold outreach</a>.</strong> Weekly batch of ~25 prospects in a 4-touch sequence. List sources, qualification, scripts, A/B testing.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/local-networking/">M2 &middot; Local networking</a>.</strong> Chambers, BNI, trade associations, business-coach ecosystem. Cadence and follow-up.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/social-media/">M3 &middot; Social media</a>.</strong> Two-platform organic presence, repurposing rhythm, posting cadence, 30-minute daily cap. Zero paid promotion.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/content-marketing-ops/">M4 &middot; Content marketing ops</a>.</strong> Bi-weekly publishing cadence, topic ideation, repurposing workflow.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/email-newsletter/">M5 &middot; Email newsletter</a>.</strong> List segments, bi-weekly cadence, tip/ship/ask template, compliance.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/reviews-and-testimonials/">M6 &middot; Reviews &amp; testimonials</a>.</strong> When to ask, channel mix, scripts, response policy, un-hide trigger.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/case-studies-and-pr/">M7 &middot; Case studies &amp; PR</a>.</strong> One per quarter; permissions, interview script, pitching trade press.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/partner-program/">M8 &middot; Partner program</a>.</strong> Three tiers, outreach pitch, onboarding, quarterly check-ins.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/retention-and-upsell/">M9 &middot; Retention &amp; upsell</a>.</strong> Triggers, QBR template, upsell catalog, win-back sequence.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/annual-planning/">M10 &middot; Annual planning</a>.</strong> Q1 plan, KPI dashboard, channel allocation, capacity ceiling.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/sop/landing-page-playbook/">M11 &middot; Landing-page playbook</a>.</strong> Standard structure, tracking, expiry handling for any new campaign page.</li>
</ol>

